WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.837 --> 00:00:04.239
The filling unit on line 3 in hall B is running.

2
00:00:04.939 --> 00:00:07.632
It fills the cartons with product from the tank.

3
00:00:08.665 --> 00:00:09.896
You are the engineer.

4
00:00:10.687 --> 00:00:13.508
With the team lead you keep it going for a whole shift.

5
00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:16.403
That shift needs four things.

6
00:00:17.121 --> 00:00:21.290
Pace, good cartons, a unit that stays whole and safe work.

7
00:00:22.377 --> 00:00:23.991
That makes four stations.

8
00:00:24.692 --> 00:00:27.908
From capacity and quality to maintenance and safety.

9
00:00:29.193 --> 00:00:31.782
The first station is Capacity and flow.

10
00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:35.378
Line 3 must make enough cartons for the customer.

11
00:00:36.418 --> 00:00:38.043
The customer sets the pace.

12
00:00:38.747 --> 00:00:41.417
Every minute of stoppage is a minute behind.

13
00:00:42.451 --> 00:00:45.632
You work out the takt time and keep a downtime log.

14
00:00:46.658 --> 00:00:51.326
Without this nobody knows what pace the line must keep, or where the minutes go.

15
00:00:52.624 --> 00:00:54.644
The second station is Quality.

16
00:00:55.417 --> 00:00:57.994
Every carton that leaves the line must be good.

17
00:00:59.068 --> 00:01:01.634
At the end of the belt you watch for faults.

18
00:01:02.352 --> 00:01:04.291
A bad carton is set apart.

19
00:01:05.387 --> 00:01:09.346
You note faults on a check sheet and write a nonconformance report.

20
00:01:10.411 --> 00:01:15.461
Without this nobody knows what goes wrong, and a bad carton can reach the customer.

21
00:01:16.761 --> 00:01:18.886
The third station is Maintenance.

22
00:01:19.585 --> 00:01:22.371
The unit has to stay whole, shift after shift.

23
00:01:23.403 --> 00:01:26.689
At the start of the shift you walk a round past the unit.

24
00:01:27.445 --> 00:01:29.303
Anything that is off gets a tag.

25
00:01:30.306 --> 00:01:34.799
You follow a CILT standard and log what you find in the CMMS.

26
00:01:35.826 --> 00:01:39.193
Without this wear can go unnoticed until the line stops.

27
00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:43.091
The fourth station is Safety on the floor.

28
00:01:43.824 --> 00:01:46.807
When the unit jams, someone has to get at it.

29
00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:49.650
Before you start you look around.

30
00:01:50.477 --> 00:01:54.204
Then the energy goes off at the switch, with a lock and a tag.

31
00:01:55.239 --> 00:01:57.677
You do an LMRA and apply LOTO.

32
00:01:58.741 --> 00:02:01.887
Without this the unit can start while your hands are in it.

33
00:02:03.265 --> 00:02:04.426
This is the whole map.

34
00:02:05.173 --> 00:02:08.935
The four stations of Keeping the plant running lie in one zone.

35
00:02:09.945 --> 00:02:15.274
First Capacity and flow, from takt and line balance to changeover and batch size.

36
00:02:16.395 --> 00:02:20.331
Then Quality, from tolerances and measuring to risk and control.

37
00:02:21.337 --> 00:02:25.308
Then Maintenance, from maintenance strategies to measuring maintenance.

38
00:02:26.353 --> 00:02:31.844
Finally Safety on the floor, from risk and controls to incidents and safety culture.

39
00:02:32.915 --> 00:02:34.308
That is how they connect.

40
00:02:35.048 --> 00:02:39.540
The customer sets the pace, and quality makes sure every carton is good.

41
00:02:40.681 --> 00:02:42.481
Maintenance keeps the unit whole.

42
00:02:43.194 --> 00:02:45.168
Safety decides how you work on it.

43
00:02:46.212 --> 00:02:49.474
Each station is a module with four levels per topic.

44
00:02:50.271 --> 00:02:52.210
Start with what your line needs now.
